## Academic Collaboration Clause

This repository is part of a research program in which empirical validation
is intended to be conducted in collaboration with academic institutions
(universities, research labs). The following terms apply to institutional
collaborators:

**Permitted under this clause:**

- Use of the framework, code, and documentation for non-commercial academic
  research, subject to a signed **Memorandum of Understanding (MoU)** and
  **Data-Sharing Agreement** with the principal investigator (JP Chancay).
- Collection and analysis of experimental data using the L3 infrastructure,
  provided the data is shared with the PI under the terms of the
  Data-Sharing Agreement before any publication.
- Co-authorship on resulting papers, conditional on substantive contribution
  as defined in the MoU.

**Reserved by this clause:**

- **Principal Investigator (PI) status** is retained by Juan Pablo Chancay
  for any work originating from or building directly upon this repository.
- **First authorship** on the primary L3 paper is retained by JP Chancay.
  Institutional co-authors appear in order of contribution as defined in
  the MoU.
- **IP over the composition operator C** and any CAL-L3 theoretical
  contributions remains with JP Chancay unless explicitly transferred in
  writing.

**How to initiate collaboration:**

Open an issue in this repository with the subject "Collaboration Inquiry —
[Institution Name]" or contact via the CAL framework repository:
<https://github.com/jpcpol/Cognitive-Abstraction-Layer-CAL>

